1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dona Guiomar de Sá38,39,292,55,212,9,12,294,39,292,293,12,231 was also known as Dona Guiomar de Sáa.307 She was born circa 1450.9 She was Dama do Paço.218 She married Fernão Alvares da Maia after 1522 at Madeira.39
2 CONC ,305 She left a will on 1 Aug 1543.218 She died in 1547 at São Miguel.299,12,218 She was buried in the chancel of São Sebastião (Matriz), Ponta Delgada, with her husband Gaspar.299
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Gaspard de Bettencourt (I) o Francês and Dona Guiomar de Sá were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 75 i. Henrique de Bettencourt was born circa 1475 at São Miguel. He married Dona Maria de Azevedo, daughter of Manuel de Oliveira, at Évora.
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 76 ii. João de Bettencourt e Sá was born circa 1475 at Madeira. He married Dona Guiomar de Sãopayo, daughter of Goncallo Vaz Botelho o Moço, at São Miguel.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 77 iii. Rafael de Bettencourt e Sáa308,292,224,309,310,292,309 was also known as Rafael Betancur.292 He was also known as Rafael de Bettencourt.310 He was born after 1477 at São Miguel.292,309 In contradiction to other sources, 
2 CONC according to Genealogias de S. Miguel e Santa Maria, Rafael, although dull-witted, married Margarida Gonçalves who made a will 18 Dec 1555, while her husband was still living. Nevertheless, all sources agree that he died childless
2 CONC . Genealogias also states that Rafael was illegitimate, not the son of Guiomar de Sá.310,309 He died after 18 Dec 1555.310,292,224
2 CONT
2 CONT * 78 iv. Dona Brites de Sá292,292,311,312,9,292,288,312,9 was also known as Dona Beatriz de Sá.312,294 She was also known as Brites de Bettencourt.9 She was also known as Brites de Bettencourt e Sáa.308 She was born circa 1475 at 
2 CONC Madeira.292,9 The three sisters, Brites, Guimar, and Isabel moved to Lisbon.304 King João III, reigned 1521-1557, lived between 1502 and 1557.313 Dona Brites was brought up with King João III.312 She married Pedro Lasso la Vega at
2 CONC  Castile.292,301,312,9,294 She was Lady-in-waiting to Queen D. Maria, second wife of D. Manuel I, o Venturoso at Lisboa.304 King Manuel I gave her six moios of wheat each year as a pension, produce from the land of Martin Vaz, acc
2 CONC ountant. Later, after her death, this favor was transferred to her sister, Dona Izabel.312 She and Pedro Lasso la Vega had no children.292,312,294 She was the prettiest lady of the Portuguese Court, having ballads that are dedicat
2 CONC ed to her in the Cancioneiro de Garcia de Resende.294 She was a lady-in-waiting of the Empress Isabel, wife of Charles V of Spain, Holy Roman Emperor at Castile.301,312,294 She witnessed the move of Isabella of Portugal, to marry 
2 CONC Charles V of Spain, Holy Roman Emperor on 11 Mar 1526 at Castile.314 By the missive of 2 Dec 1526, D. João III made her a grant of the white and black soap factories of São Miguel, the same way that his brother Henrique had done a
2 CONC nd conceded other grants to her.294 She died at Castile.292
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro Lasso la Vega315 was also known as Pedro Lasso de Vega.294 He was also known as Pedro Lasso de Lavega.292 He was also known as Pedro Laço de la Vega.304 He was also known as Pedro Lasso da Veiga.312 He was also known as Pedr
2 CONC o Lasso de La Vega.9 He was born circa 1470 at Castile.292 Pedro Lasso la Vega was Lord of Arcos Brateris, and Carcos.292,304 His titles were confiscated to be Head of the Comunidades of Castile.292,304 His titles were restored by
2 CONC  his marriage through the influence of the Empress.292,316,312 He married Isabel de Bettencourt e Sáa (brother- and sister-in-law), daughter of Gaspard de Bettencourt (I) o Francês and Dona Guiomar de Sá, at Castile.292,301,312,9,
2 CONC 317 He and Isabel de Bettencourt e Sáa had no children.292,312,317
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 79 v. Dona Guiomar de Sá was born circa 1475 at Madeira. She married António Juzarte de Mello, son of Pedro Juzarte, at Madeira. She married Dom Fernando de Castro at São Miguel. She married Diogo Juzarte de Monte Mor o Velho 
2 CONC at Madeira.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 80 vi. Isabel de Bettencourt e Sáa308,292,318,312,9,292,288,312,9 was also known as Dona Izabel de Sá.292,319,320 She was also known as Isabel de Bettencourt.9 She was also known as Isabel de Sá.294 She was born circa 1475 at Ma
2 CONC deira.292,9 The three sisters, Brites, Guimar, and Isabel moved to Lisbon.304 Isabel de Bettencourt e Sáa was chief lady-in-waiting who brought up the Queen of Bohemia, wife of Emperor Maximilian II.292,321 She was a lady-in-waiti
2 CONC ng of the Empress Isabel, wife of Charles V of Spain, Holy Roman Emperor at Castile.301,312,294 She witnessed the move of Isabella of Portugal, to marry Charles V of Spain, Holy Roman Emperor on 11 Mar 1526 at Castile.314 She marr
2 CONC ied Dom Fernando Sanegos at Castile (he was her sister's widowed husband).301,9,294 She and Pedro Lasso la Vega had no children.292,312,317 She married Pedro Lasso la Vega (brother- and sister-in-law) at Castile.292,301,312,9,317 
2 CONC She gave the land for the chapel of Corpo Santo in Ponta Delgada.317 She died in 1574 at Castile.299,294
2 CONT
2 CONT Dom Fernando Sanegos301,9 was born circa 1500 at Madeira Islands.315
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedro Lasso la Vega315 was also known as Pedro Lasso de Vega.294 He was also known as Pedro Lasso de Lavega.292 He was also known as Pedro Laço de la Vega.304 He was also known as Pedro Lasso da Veiga.312 He was also known as Pedr
2 CONC o Lasso de La Vega.9 He was born circa 1470 at Castile.292 Pedro Lasso la Vega was Lord of Arcos Brateris, and Carcos.292,304 His titles were confiscated to be Head of the Comunidades of Castile.292,304 He married Dona Brites de S
2 CONC á, daughter of Gaspard de Bettencourt (I) o Francês and Dona Guiomar de Sá, at Castile.292,301,312,9,294 He and Dona Brites de Sá had no children.292,312,294 His titles were restored by his marriage through the influence of the Em
2 CONC press.292,316,312
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 81 vii. Margarida de Bettencourt e Sáa was born circa 1480 at Madeira. She married Pedro Rodrigues da Câmara, son of Rui Gonçalves da Câmara and Maria Rodrigues, at São Miguel.
