1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afonso_de_Albuquerque '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT * D. Afonso de Albuquerque (Alhandra, 1453 — Goa, 16 de Dezembro de 1515) foi um militar e político português, uma das principais figuras da expansão portuguesa no Oriente e da afirmação de Portugal como grande potência asiática e
2 CONC nquanto governador da Índia Portuguesa.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afonso_de_Albuquerque
2 CONT
2 CONT Afonso de Albuquerque (or archaically spelt as Aphonso d'Albuquerque and also spelt as Alfonso, and Alphonso; Portuguese pronunciation: [ɐˈfõsu dɨ aɫbuˈkɛɾk]; 1453 – December 16, 1515), 1st Duke of Goa, was a Portuguese fidalgo, o
2 CONC r nobleman, an admiral whose military and administrative activities as second governor of Portuguese India conquered and established the Portuguese colonial empire in the Indian Ocean.
2 CONT
2 CONT After finishing his education, Albuquerque first served in North Africa and in the Mediterranean where he took part in numerous successful campaigns against the Arabs and the Ottomans. His long military career in these fronts mean
2 CONC t he had acquired the military experience needed to operate in the newly reached and vastly unexplored Indian Ocean.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is generally considered a world conquest military genius, given his successful strategy: he attempted to close all the Indian Ocean naval passages to the Atlantic, Red Sea, Persian Gulf, and to the Pacific, transforming it into
2 CONC  a Portuguese mare clausum established over the Ottoman power and their Muslim and Hindu allies.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was responsible for building numerous fortresses to defend key strategic positions and establishing a net of diplomatic relations. Albuquerque was appointed "Governor and Captain-General of India" and shortly before his death "
2 CONC Duke of Goa", the first Portuguese nobility title landed overseas, by king Manuel I of Portugal, becoming the first Portuguese duke not from the royal family. He was one of the first to commission secure trading relations with Chi
2 CONC na during the Ming Dynasty, also either establishing or improving commercial trades with Siam, Ethiopia, and Persia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albuquerque was known as a prodigious maritime commander, who would often engage with and defeat much larger armies and fleets. For example his capture of Ormuz in 1507 against the Persians was accomplished with an army fifty time
2 CONC s smaller. Other famous battles and offensives lead by Albuquerque include the conquest of Goa in 1510 and the capture of Malacca in 1511.
2 CONT
2 CONT Centuries after Alexander the Great, he was the first European whose dream of establishing an empire in India, or in Asia for any matter, controlled from abroad, was successfully accomplished. His military and diplomatic contribut
2 CONC ions are generally regarded as one of the most vital to help the Portuguese create a colonial empire in Asia as well as reaching the spice routes in the South East Asia and the South West Pacific. He became known as The Terrible, 
2 CONC The Great, The Caesar of the East, Lion of the Seas, and as The Portuguese Mars.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============================================
2 CONT
2 CONT SOUSA, Manuel de Faria e, 1590-1649 Asia portuguesa. Tomo I NÚMERO 1
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/res-752-a_0000_capa-capa_t24-C-R0150/page/n216/mode/1up 
2 CONT  https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afonso_de_Albuquerque
2 CONT https://archive.li/FaEbL 
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/affonso-de-albuquerque/Affonso%20de%20Albuquerque2.png 
2 CONT Afonso de Albuquerque (c. 1452–1462[1] – Goa, 16
2 CONT de Dezembro de 1515), cognominado o Grande, o
2 CONT César do Oriente, o Leão dos Mares, o Terribil e o
2 CONT Marte Português 
2 CONT    Filho de Gonçalo de Albuquerque c/c Leonor de Menezes, foi um fidalgo português, falecido antes de 1515, conhecido genealogicamente como o pai do famoso navegador e administrador colonial Afonso de Albuquerque, o "Grandioso", q
2 CONC ue estabeleceu o domínio português na Índia
2 CONT . Era filho de João de Albuquerque e de Leonor Lopes Gonçalves Leão, pertencendo a uma linhagem nobre. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Pai de Afonso de Albuquerque: Sua maior relevância histórica documentada é ser o progenitor de Afonso de Albuquerque, cuja mãe foi Leonor de Menezes.
2 CONT     Contexto Familiar: A família Albuquerque tem raízes profundas na nobreza portuguesa, sendo ancestral de diversos ramos importantes em Portugal e no Nordeste brasileiro.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
