1 NOTE Pedro Fajardo was a Adelantado Mayor de Murcia. In 1457 Pedro empowered his wife, Leonor to administer three villas in Murcia. In 1481 Pedro fajardo regained what his ancestors had lost, the Senority Cartagena which was an importa
2 CONC nt port. His son in law was Juan Chacon. During this time there was a civil war between Spain and Portugal, Enrique and Isabella. After Enrique died the war continued via his daughter. A Jew seems to have funded some of the war. M
2 CONC osen Ruano, who was also suspected being a spy. He was detained in Avila, brought before judges on 12 October 1478 despite having furnished papers brought from Portugal to give to his Castillian contacts. He was tortured until he 
2 CONC was close to almost dying. He was set free upon the judgemnent that he really had nothing to divulge of impprtance.
2 CONT ES.47161.AGS/1.1.31.1.1124.3//RGS,148310,213
2 CONT Titulo Nombre atribuido:
2 CONT Receptoría en pleito de Leonor Manrique sobre el lugar de Fortuna.
2 CONT Fecha Creacion:
2 CONT 1483-10-30, (Vitoria) -
2 CONT Receptoría en el pleito de Dona Leonor Manrique mujer que fue del adelantado D. Juan Fajardo, D. Juan Chacon adelantado mayor del reino de Murcia y consortes, con D. Juan de Cascales vecino y regidor de Murcia, sobre razon del lug
2 CONC ar de Fortuna.-Consejo.
